	(text "Cross to H7 UART: ESP_UART_TX -> H7_RX, ESP_UART_RX -> H7_TX.\nH7 idles its TX (ESP_UART_RX) high. Enter download mode:\nESP_BOOT low + pulse ESP_EN low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9ef768b8-afa6-4bc5-b04a-f7b9f327578a")
	)
	(text "Reserved for future USB connector\n(native USB-Serial/JTAG flashing/debug)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 153.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c00f6ee2-6c60-467a-b6be-21b7e2ef841b")
	)
	(text "3V3 rail must supply >=500 mA peaks (Wi-Fi TX). Place C6 closer to pin 1 than C1.\nSPI is ESP32-C3 SPI2 in slave mode, up to 60 MHz. Keep traces short, length-matched.\nGPIO11-17 not available (in-package flash)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "cf0ecb06-73b5-48e3-aa61-39b0ae899255")
	)
	(text "H7 drives open-drain or push-pull-LOW only. EN is shared with the\nR12/C7 power-on-reset RC, so the H7 must never source current into it\n(a push-pull high would override the RC delay and fight any pull-down\non the net)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d3859b3d-aaba-4e5d-a261-26ab992562f8")
	)
